# Copy to `apps/dashboard/.env`. Unlike the rest of this workspace, the dashboard does NOT
# read the root .env: Next loads .env files from the application directory only, and none of
# these variables belong to the API or the database anyway.
#
# Everything here is `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, which means it is substituted into the JavaScript the
# browser downloads at build time. Nothing secret can go in this file. There is nothing
# secret to put in it either — the dashboard holds no credential of its own; the access
# token lives in memory for the life of a tab and the refresh token is a cookie the browser
# will only ever hand back to the API.

# Where apps/api is. Required for a production build — `next build` fails rather than
# shipping a bundle that calls localhost. Outside production it defaults to the port the API
# listens on, so a fresh checkout runs `pnpm dev` unchanged.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What the API has to be told, for any of this to work
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are apps/api's settings, not this app's. They are listed here because a dashboard
# that cannot sign in looks like a bug in the dashboard, and all three of these produce that
# symptom. Set them in apps/api/.env (or the root .env).
#
#   CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3001
#       The browser calls the API cross-origin with `credentials: 'include'`. Without this
#       origin listed, the API sends no CORS headers at all and every call fails as an
#       indistinguishable network error. Port 3001 is what `pnpm dev` serves this app on.
#
#   OAUTH_WEB_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001
#       Where a completed sign-in lands. apps/api builds every post-sign-in redirect as
#       `OAUTH_WEB_BASE_URL + returnTo` and there is exactly ONE of them, shared by the
#       storefront and the dashboard — so while working on the dashboard it must point here,
#       and while working on apps/web it must point there. See src/lib/auth/sign-in-url.ts
#       for the fix this deployment-time workaround is standing in for.
#
#   COOKIE_SECURE=false
#       A laptop has no TLS terminator, and every cookie in the flow is `Secure` by default.
#       The API refuses this value unless OAUTH_CALLBACK_BASE_URL is a loopback address, so
#       it cannot be the thing production forgot.
#
#   OAUTH_<PROVIDER>_CLIENT_ID / _CLIENT_SECRET
#       At least one, or the sign-in page correctly renders "no provider is configured".
#       There are no real credentials in this repository.

# ── Where the customer-facing shop is ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Used for the "ดูหน้าร้าน" link on a published product, so a staff member can check their
# own work. Unset outside development means no link is shown — a link to the wrong origin is
# worse than none, because it is followed and read as a failed publish.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002
